  "prompts": {
    "common": "You propose a bounded linear response/defer rule, not code. A qualified event visit and a routine head have already passed the same ownership, reservation, horizon, revisit-return and extra-visit-budget checker. If both differ and are legal, score = bias + risk_weight*(public_risk/4) + age_weight*(event_age_seconds/120) + extra_time_weight*((event_finish-head_finish)/300) + slack_difference_weight*((event_min_slack-head_min_slack)/600). Score>=0 responds to the fixed FIFO event; score<0 executes the routine head without closing the event. Forced or identical actions are outside your control. Four weights must each be finite in[-4,4], bias finite in[-2,2]. Zero weights and zero bias reproduceFIFO. Return exactly one JSON object with version1,bias,andweights{risk,age,extra_time,slack_difference}. No code,markdown,explanations,extra keys,task IDs or future labels. The study optimizes confirmed abnormal intervals while preserving revisit constraints and limiting travel and completion costs. The common known baseline comes from12 previously seen synthetic thermal-cooling processes. Uncalibrated risk is not a failure probability. Task score is not minimized: positive gate score means respond. Do not change TTL,people,estimator,qualifications,budget or certificate. Repeated conditions or candidates are not independent experiments.",
